#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5dd8e22-4e53-5097-9663-141d62fb9e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5dd8e22-4e53-5097-9663-141d62fb9e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303640} :answer-field/id #uuid "d17d2d99-482a-5e96-a7f8-10615a206c45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7e6a604d-c591-56e2-a8f3-63cd2a5f1e21" :question/math-academy-id "q-347182" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )+\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3})-(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db6c166e-72c3-552d-b524-d11113f0a364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309032} {:answer/id #uuid "76d59c68-af09-5e9e-a3c5-93ed10ab20f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db6c166e-72c3-552d-b524-d11113f0a364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309032} :answer-field/id #uuid "98143ef5-3ba7-5bf3-8e38-a70e9df4babe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3ea82d24-c80c-5089-8bd5-efac42e51f83" :question/math-academy-id "q-348724" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{6}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+3{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}^{2}] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bf4c878-7b92-592b-adc2-112e45c4e87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303667} {:answer/id #uuid "60640a78-8f09-5331-a704-26677847ffbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60640a78-8f09-5331-a704-26677847ffbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303668} :answer-field/id #uuid "859cec6a-b48c-5542-b4bf-ce49ea1111b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5028512b-a5ef-5c38-81c4-6a7be0e32b0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-361711" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/assets/f8aa97ff1ff27ec11df6aefd4523ed9d39efac686c777f7242701aa2f4fef79c.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2-x]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3-x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-[0] \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88151861-75ad-5e5d-a049-e83aa028ef9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309804} {:answer/id #uuid "47c6df3b-118b-536b-ab2e-a17e3c312238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309805} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd7c238-0f8c-5b16-a217-d1386176e1bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309806} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b4438a-9b6d-5673-a6b8-e8a3bc72b8fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309807} {:answer/id #uuid "90d47605-dabb-54b0-b71e-566d6f7d665f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d47605-dabb-54b0-b71e-566d6f7d665f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309808} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d94537d-95f9-5179-95cd-10d218124d7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d13285f0-0de3-5f3e-aab5-8630896b0697" :question/math-academy-id "q-49286" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/assets/0f8e4dc1dff5673d8fc95375f9632f43bc4942335899e0e6dad11e8693bd6599.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=5{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi .$ The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=5{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi $ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}([\\pi -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )]-[0-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b1df459-e9e7-5e24-ae93-8f0ff084df92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309064} {:answer/id #uuid "927025b0-c583-5026-b39b-a84e6e40b2d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309065} {:answer/id #uuid "718e047b-bdee-561c-a8c7-ab2fa2e7ff19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309066} {:answer/id #uuid "519c467f-ada4-539f-8dfb-7981817b82dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309067} {:answer/id #uuid "ac2ffba9-fc21-5cdd-a62e-13a587b0f243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1df459-e9e7-5e24-ae93-8f0ff084df92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309064} :answer-field/id #uuid "9503887d-706b-5511-bfd5-17f38263336e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12b0a367-b2dc-50bf-a676-57aa1201b034" :question/math-academy-id "q-74403" :question/problem "$\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [3({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
